@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Wi-Fi health dashboard
+
+A dedicated 240×320 LVGL application for the ESP32-C3 / 8 MB FoloToy AI Passport.
+
+- Five pages: overview, latest valid pressure with its original measurement time, seven nights of staged sleep with today's score, workout types and totals, and daily activity.
+- An SNTP-calibrated UTC+8 clock updates locally. A clock tick does not make an HTTP request.
+- Two 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi profiles and a dedicated read-only HTTPS credential are stored in NVS; health snapshots stay in RAM.
+- Poll every 30 minutes. Short OK refreshes with a 15-second minimum interval; UP/DOWN change pages.
+- Hold OK for about half a second to configure Wi-Fi. Join the displayed Health-XXXX network and open http://192.168.4.1.
+- Configure home Wi-Fi and an iPhone hotspot; enable Maximum Compatibility on the hotspot. Failed candidate profiles roll back after 45 seconds.
+- After 60 idle seconds, turn the backlight off and stop LVGL timers. Any function key only wakes; a subsequent gesture acts normally. Setup stays awake.
+- Network updates continue with the screen off and never wake it. CPU deep sleep is not enabled. Battery runtime has not been measured.
+- API OFFLINE / LAST DATA retains the original snapshot date. Missing values are not zero; retained pressure keeps its original time.
+
+Data path: Apple Health → HealthRelay service → dedicated private Base cache → authenticated read-only Magic FaaS → badge.
+See [HealthRelay badge documentation](https://github.com/Julian0197/health-relay/blob/master/docs/ai-passport-health.md) for the complete deployment, permissions, local synthetic debug mode and bootstrap instructions.
+
+```sh
+# Activate ESP-IDF 5.5.3 first.
+./tools/validate.sh --all
+python3 tools/configure_wifi.py --config /absolute/private-data/badge.json --port /dev/cu.usbmodemXXXX
+```
+
+The owner-only JSON contains only url and token. Never put credentials in arguments, source or firmware images. Ordinary NVS has no flash encryption.
+HTTPS uses certificate validation after clock synchronization, rejects redirects, and caps responses at 4093 bytes.
+Flash a verified merged image for first installation. Before an application-only update, verify identical partition tables; never write an application image at 0x0. Do not erase the whole chip.
+Report build, host tests and device observations separately. Verify extended reconnect, unplugged polling and battery discharge on your own hardware.
